llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: a store to a non-aliasing spill slot gets no chain edge to an unknown load (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION after register allocation, in the
post-RA list scheduler: r259673 (llvm-project ac29f01788e3, 2016-02-03,
first release LLVM 3.9) rewrote ScheduleDAGInstrs' memory dependencies and
added a chain edge from a store to a stack slot that aliases nothing to a
later load of unknown memory, which keeps a spill ahead of an independent
copy. The base places the copy first (`mov r14, rdi` before `vmovss
[rbp-0x14], xmm0`: 0x968760, equal in the prebuilt 3.7.1's and 3.8.1's
modules). This patch takes back that edge alone. With it 0x968760 and
0xedede0 compile to the base's bytes, six functions of the module change
(none away from the base) and no matched game row changes. A census of the
exact shape in the game region finds five copy-first sites and three
spill-first; none of the three is in a function the tree has written.

diff -ru a/lib/CodeGen/ScheduleDAGInstrs.cpp b/lib/CodeGen/ScheduleDAGInstrs.cpp
--- a/lib/CodeGen/ScheduleDAGInstrs.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/ScheduleDAGInstrs.cpp
@@ -1002,8 +1002,15 @@
         }
         // The store may have dependencies to unanalyzable loads and
         // stores.
-        addChainDependencies(SU, Loads, UnknownValue);
-        addChainDependencies(SU, Stores, UnknownValue);
+        // PS4: not when every underlying object of the store is non-aliasing, as before r259673
+        // (ac29f01788e3, first in 3.9): not taken.
+        bool AnyMayAlias = false;
+        for (const UnderlyingObject &UnderlObj : Objs)
+          AnyMayAlias |= UnderlObj.mayAlias();
+        if (AnyMayAlias) {
+          addChainDependencies(SU, Loads, UnknownValue);
+          addChainDependencies(SU, Stores, UnknownValue);
+        }
       }
     } else { // SU is a load.
       if (Objs.empty()) {
